    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"finding small anchors\" sounds nice in theory, but it feels like just delaying the inevitable. it's like trying to build a sandcastle while the tide is coming in. if the truth is that none of it matters, then trying to find \"value\" in the small things just feels like a lie we tell ourselves so we don't have to face the void. if nothing matters, isn't a quiet exit actually a more honest way to live than pretending to care about things that won't matter in a hundred years?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
